### tb470 - x230v2-28GS (S/N A10783G262900002) on /dev/u0, bound as swi_a, for the
### PRISTINE AWPTCM 5700 bootloader suite (bootloader 6.2.40), 2026-10-06.
### The only file in this run dir that is not a byte-for-byte copy of
### claude/raw-data/test_scripts/5700_bootloader/ (Feb 2026 x230v2 control run).
### Shape = tftp_boot_over_usb_adapter.setup, as rigged for the IE520 on tb470 in
### 2026-08 (IE520/automated-bootloader/tb470-u4.setup has the reasoning).

[power]
### PDU outlet A = 1 (bench-setup/tb470.static)
pwr_a = (pdu, 10.36.150.14, 1)

[switch]
swi_a = /dev/u0

[baudrates]
### 9600: the Test Engineer set the unit to 9600 (2026-10-06); 2005's factory
### restore reverts the bootloader to 9600 and the framework never renegotiates.
swi_a = 9600

[powerlink]
swi_a = pwr_a

### Device TFTP boots over the USB ethernet adapter on a hub (the 28GS has one
### USB port; the hub carries both the adapter and the USB stick).
[hub]
hub_a = tb, swi_a

[portlink]
### Post-bootup CLI file-transfer link: tb470 eth3 (10.38.215.65/27) <-> port1.0.1
### (cabled by the Test Engineer 2026-10-06 13:1x). configure() TFTPs the release
### into flash over this; without it the framework tries `eth0` from the CLI.
tb-swi_a = eth3-port1.0.1

### Bootloader TFTP boot link: tb470 eth2 (10.38.215.33/27) <-> the USB ethernet
### adapter on the hub, which the bootloader calls eth0 (link only during boot).
### Bootloader address = eth2 network + 2 + tty = 10.38.215.34.
hub_a-tb = eth2
hub_a-swi_a = eth0
